; ISSUE-0037 -- the boot's own sequence, in a loop.
;
; Startup-Sequence:151-155 verbatim, minus the guard on ENV:SYS/Packages and
; minus the package startup it drives, so that what repeats is the RAM: file
; traffic and nothing else. Two create/write/delete cycles per iteration: T:P
; here, and Execute's own T:TmpNNNNN temporary.
;
; The names vary deliberately. muddy_pool holds file data blocks and name
; strings and nothing else, and the crash was freeing a name string, so a
; fixed-length name would probe one allocation size forever.

Echo "[ram-stress-c] start"

Lab loop

Echo "[ram-stress-c] ."

List "SYS:C" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:P" LFORMAT="; %N"
Execute "T:P"
Delete "T:P" QUIET

List "SYS:C" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:PackagesList" LFORMAT="; %N"
Execute "T:PackagesList"
Delete "T:PackagesList" QUIET

List "SYS:Libs" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:a" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:a" QUIET

List "SYS:Libs" NOHEAD FILES TO "T:a-considerably-longer-name-than-that" LFORMAT="; %N"
Delete "T:a-considerably-longer-name-than-that" QUIET

Skip loop BACK
